ADRs are written when the decision is actually made, not before.
  - build system, boot protocol: write the ADR after M0.0/M1.0, recording
    what you hit. Cheap to reverse; discovery is the right method.
  - capability representation: due at M2.1. Retype creates objects, so
    M2.1 decides this whether or not it is written down.
  - IPC message shape: due at M3.3, sized against a real workload.

